```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  [1023:0] in,
    input  [7:0]    sel,
    output [3:0]    out
);

    // sel * 4 gives the starting bit index of the selected 4-bit chunk
    assign out = in[{sel, 2'b00} +: 4];

endmodule
```

The implementation uses a variable-based indexed part-select: `{sel, 2'b00}` computes `sel * 4` (the base bit index), and `+: 4` selects the 4 consecutive bits starting there, so `sel=0` picks `in[3:0]`, `sel=1` picks `in[7:4]`, and so on up to `sel=255` picking `in[1023:1020]`.
